# An unclosed `datetime(` or `timespan(` ends at the end of its line.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | where d > datetime(2024-01-01
| where e > timespan(1:00
| take 1
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..74
  PIPELINE@0..73
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    WHERE_OP@9..38
      IDENT@9..14 "where"
      WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
      BIN_EXPR@15..38
        NAME_REF@15..16
          IDENT@15..16 "d"
        WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
        GT@17..18 ">"
        WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
        LITERAL@19..38
          DATETIME@19..38 "datetime(2024-01-01"
    WHITESPACE@38..39 "\n"
    PIPE@39..40 "|"
    WHITESPACE@40..41 " "
    WHERE_OP@41..64
      IDENT@41..46 "where"
      WHITESPACE@46..47 " "
      BIN_EXPR@47..64
        NAME_REF@47..48
          IDENT@47..48 "e"
        WHITESPACE@48..49 " "
        GT@49..50 ">"
        WHITESPACE@50..51 " "
        LITERAL@51..64
          TIMESPAN@51..64 "timespan(1:00"
    WHITESPACE@64..65 "\n"
    PIPE@65..66 "|"
    WHITESPACE@66..67 " "
    TAKE_OP@67..73
      IDENT@67..71 "take"
      WHITESPACE@71..72 " "
      LITERAL@72..73
        LONG@72..73 "1"
  WHITESPACE@73..74 "\n"

error[DS0003]: `datetime(` is never closed
  --> query:1:20
  |
1 | from t | where d > datetime(2024-01-01
  |                    ^^^^^^^^^ this literal has no closing `)` on this line
  |
  = help: close it with `)`: `datetime(2024-01-01)`

error[DS0003]: `timespan(` is never closed
  --> query:2:13
  |
2 | | where e > timespan(1:00
  |             ^^^^^^^^^ this literal has no closing `)` on this line
  |
  = help: close it with `)`: `timespan(1:00)`
